<title>JAPAN: Kyushu Electric nuclear plant to start up Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Kyushu Electric nuclear plant to start up Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kyushu Electric Power Co Inc said on Monday that its 1.18-million-kilowatt nuclear power plant in Genkai, western Japan, was due to begin generating electricity on a trial basis on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The company said it expected the No.4 light-water reactor to begin commercial operations in July 1997, after it receives approval to do so from the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI).</p>
</text>
